The reference image for Anthracnose (`Mango_Leaf_383.jpg`) shows distinct dark, irregularly shaped spots with defined margins, which are different from the diffuse, powdery patches on the test image. This confirms that Anthracnose is not the correct classification.

Based on the visual evidence from the test image and the comparisons with the 8 reference images, Powdery_Mildew consistently matches the appearance of the test image with its characteristic light, powdery patches. The other diseases (Sooty_Mould, Anthracnose, Die_Back) show distinct symptoms that do not align with the test image.

